※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=7
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ Two questions, and not the same one.  `visible` decides whether the finished
※ image offers a symbol; `export` decides whether a file importing this module
※ may name the definition.  Nothing here imports this file, so what is only
※ exported is something nothing reaches, and it is not in the image at all.
@[visible]
let shared: u6 = 7u6

@[export]
let lent: u6 = 8u6

let private: u6 = 9u6

@[visible]
fn reachable() → u6:
    1u6

@[export]
fn lendable() → u6:
    2u6

fn unreachable() → u6:
    3u6

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    shared
